      "writtenOn": "2025-05-07T10:42:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If we define a \"cutoff\" timestamp for updating the change cache, then it would also work in your case. E.g. You define a \"cutoff\" timestamp to _now +1day_ and therefore none of the changes updates will be persisted.\n\nThat would also work for other online cases, not only for offline reindexing.\n\nIn our case, we\u0027ll set to _now -1week_ and only the updates of the last week until now will trigger a change cache refresh.\n\nWhat do you think?",
      "parentUuid": "b531f78c_12e078a6",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 103,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 104,
        "endChar": 33
      },
      "revId": "fa3d331b08c3bb4a8c0ebf8e41eacc7530f1780d",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "fd645a13_e1de2aeb",
        "filename": "java/com/google/gerrit/pgm/Reindex.java",
        "patchSetId": 11
      },
      "lineNbr": 104,
      "author": {
        "id": 1065256
